language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ eighteen_hole_golf: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Generate an 18-hole golf course where each hole has a length of 3, 4, or 5, and the total length of the course is 72.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/eighteen_hole_golf.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the number of holes and the total length of the course
letting n_holes = 18
letting course_length = 72
$ holes[h]: the length of hole h, of 3, 4 or 5, indices 1-based (hole 1 is the first hole)
find holes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_holes)] of int(3..5)

such that
$ the total length of the course is 72
(sum h : int(1..n_holes) . holes[h]) = course_length
